---
/* The hundred and fifty-four.

   Pazin's own register list is the only source in this archive that records
   whether a volume has been photographed. A hundred and fifty-four of its
   entries say no — and those are not a gap in anybody's website, they are books
   on a shelf that exist and cannot be read from here. This page turns that
   column into something that can be posted. */
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
import { md, mdp } from "../lib/md.js";
import registers from "../data/registers.json";
import rm from "../data/researchmap.json";

/* Which of Pazin's «not digitised» volumes somebody ELSE has filmed. Computed
   by the research-map builder, which is the only place that holds both
   catalogues side by side. */
const filmedToo = new Set(rm.stats.filmedElsewhere || []);
const covered = (r) => filmedToo.has(r.dapa_no);

const TYPE = { MKR: "Births", MKV: "Marriages", MKU: "Deaths", SD: "Church census" };
const rows = registers.filter(r => r.digitised !== "yes");

/* Grouped by who holds the paper, because that is who gets the letter. One
   request to DAPA covers a hundred and eighteen volumes; a parish office
   holding four is a different letter and a different tone. */
const byHolder = {};
for (const r of rows) (byHolder[r.held_at || "unrecorded"] ||= []).push(r);
const holders = Object.entries(byHolder).sort((a, b) => b[1].length - a[1].length);

const byPlace = {};
for (const r of rows) (byPlace[r.place] ||= []).push(r);
const places = Object.entries(byPlace).sort((a, b) => b[1].length - a[1].length);

const ours = new Set(["Gologorica", "Gračišće", "Pićan", "Pazin", "Svetvinčenat"]);
const mine = rows.filter(r => ours.has(r.place));
const nowhere = rows.filter(r => !covered(r));
const elsewhere = rows.filter(r => covered(r));
const HOLDER = {
  DAPA: "Državni arhiv u Pazinu — the state archive itself",
  ZMP: "Zavičajni muzej Poreštine, Poreč",
  "MU Pula": "Matični ured Pula — the civil registry office",
  "BA Poreč": "Biskupijski arhiv Poreč — the diocesan archive",
};
const holderName = (h) =>
  HOLDER[h] || (h.startsWith("ŽU ") ? `Župni ured ${h.slice(3)} — the parish office itself` : h);
---
<Base
  title="The hundred and fifty-four"
  eyebrow={`${rows.length} volumes Pazin has not digitised · ${nowhere.length} of them filmed by nobody else either`}
  dek="Every register in Pazin's own list marked «not digitised» — and, for each, whether anybody else has filmed it. Most of them somebody has. The ones nobody has are the short list worth a letter.">

  <div class="one" style="border-left-color:var(--accent)">
    <div class="lab">Why this list is different from everything else here</div>
    <div class="prose" style="margin-top:8px" set:html={mdp(
`Every other source this archive uses says what it *has*. **Pazin is the only one that says what it hasn't.** Its register list carries a digitised column, and ${rows.length} of its entries say no.

That single column is worth more than the rest of the catalogue put together, because it converts an absence into an address. **FamilySearch not holding a book tells you nothing** — it might be at Pazin, it might be lost, it might never have existed. Pazin saying «not digitised» tells you the book is real, where it is, and what it is called.

**${mine.length} of the ${rows.length} are in parishes on our own line** — ${[...new Set(mine.map(r => r.place))].sort().join(", ")}.`)}></div>
  </div>

  <div class="one" style="margin-top:22px;border-left-color:var(--accent)">
    <div class="lab">And a sentence this page carried for a day that was not true</div>
    <div class="prose" style="margin-top:8px" set:html={mdp(
`This page opened by saying these were *«books that exist, on a shelf in Istria, and cannot be read from anywhere else»*. **For ${elsewhere.length} of the ${rows.length}, that is wrong.**

Pazin's column means **«not digitised by Pazin»**. It says nothing about anybody else, and checked against FamilySearch's films of the same parish, record type and years, **${elsewhere.length} of these volumes are already photographed** — often inside a longer film that swallows several of Pazin's shelfmarks at once. Barban's *Births 1716–1750*, *1750–1781* and *1781–1816* are three Pazin volumes and one FamilySearch reel.

**${nowhere.length} are left.** Those are the ones where two catalogues agree that nothing has been photographed, and they are the only ones worth a letter.

*The overlap is inferred, not proved.* Same parish, same record type, overlapping years is a strong match and not an identity — a parish copy and a diocesan copy can both exist. But it is more than enough to stop calling all 154 unreachable.`)}></div>
  </div>

  <h2 id="nowhere" style="font-size:26px;margin-top:44px">The {nowhere.length} nobody has filmed</h2>
  <p class="dek" style="margin-top:8px">Pazin has not digitised these and no film of that parish, record type and period turns up anywhere else this archive can reach. <strong>This is the list worth posting.</strong></p>
  <div class="scroll" style="margin-top:14px">
    <table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13.5px">
      <thead><tr>
        <th style="text-align:left;padding:6px 10px 6px 0">Place</th>
        <th style="text-align:left;padding:6px 10px">Register</th>
        <th style="text-align:left;padding:6px 10px">Years</th>
        <th style="text-align:left;padding:6px 10px">Held by</th>
        <th style="text-align:left;padding:6px 0 6px 10px">DAPA no.</th>
      </tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {nowhere.map(r => (
          <tr style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule)">
            <td style="padding:7px 10px 7px 0;white-space:nowrap"><strong>{r.place}</strong></td>
            <td style="padding:7px 10px">{TYPE[r.type] || r.type}</td>
            <td style="padding:7px 10px;white-space:nowrap">{r.period}</td>
            <td style="padding:7px 10px">{r.held_at}</td>
            <td style="padding:7px 0 7px 10px;color:var(--dim)">{r.dapa_no}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="ours" style="font-size:26px;margin-top:50px">Ours first</h2>
  <p class="dek" style="margin-top:8px">The {mine.length} volumes in parishes this family is actually documented in — <strong>{mine.filter(r => !covered(r)).length} of them filmed by nobody else.</strong></p>
  <div class="scroll" style="margin-top:14px">
    <table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13.5px">
      <thead><tr>
        <th style="text-align:left;padding:6px 10px 6px 0">Place</th>
        <th style="text-align:left;padding:6px 10px">Register</th>
        <th style="text-align:left;padding:6px 10px">Years</th>
        <th style="text-align:left;padding:6px 10px">Held by</th>
        <th style="text-align:left;padding:6px 0 6px 10px">DAPA no.</th>
      </tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {mine.map(r => (
          <tr style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule)">
            <td style="padding:7px 10px 7px 0;white-space:nowrap"><strong>{r.place}</strong></td>
            <td style="padding:7px 10px">{TYPE[r.type] || r.type}</td>
            <td style="padding:7px 10px;white-space:nowrap">{r.period}</td>
            <td style="padding:7px 10px">{r.held_at}</td>
            <td style="padding:7px 0 7px 10px;color:var(--dim)">{r.dapa_no}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="holders" style="font-size:26px;margin-top:50px">Who to write to, and for how many</h2>
  <p class="dek" style="margin-top:8px">One letter per holder, not one per book. The archive holds most of them; the rest are scattered across parish offices that hold two, three or four each.</p>
  <div style="margin-top:22px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px">
    {holders.map(([h, list]) => (
      <div class="one" style={list.length > 20 ? "border-left-color:var(--accent)" : ""}>
        <div class="lab">{holderName(h)} — {list.length} volume{list.length === 1 ? "" : "s"}</div>
        <p class="cap" style="margin-top:8px">
          {[...new Set(list.map(r => r.place))].sort().join(" · ")}
        </p>
        <ul style="margin:10px 0 0;padding:0;list-style:none;display:grid;gap:3px;font-size:13px">
          {list.slice(0, 12).map(r => (
            <li>{r.place} — {TYPE[r.type] || r.type} {r.period} <span class="cap">({r.dapa_no})</span></li>
          ))}
        </ul>
        {list.length > 12 && <p class="cap" style="margin-top:8px">and {list.length - 12} more, listed by place below.</p>}
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <h2 id="places" style="font-size:26px;margin-top:50px">All {rows.length}, by place</h2>
  <div style="margin-top:20px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:20px">
    {places.map(([place, list]) => (
      <div>
        <div class="lab">{place} — {list.length}</div>
        <div class="scroll" style="margin-top:8px">
          <table style="width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:13px">
            <tbody>
              {list.map(r => (
                <tr style="border-top:1px solid var(--rule)">
                  <td style="padding:5px 10px 5px 0;white-space:nowrap">{TYPE[r.type] || r.type}</td>
                  <td style="padding:5px 10px;white-space:nowrap">{r.period}</td>
                  <td style="padding:5px 10px">{r.held_at}</td>
                  <td style="padding:5px 10px;color:var(--dim);white-space:nowrap">{r.dapa_no}</td>
                  <td style="padding:5px 0 5px 10px;white-space:nowrap" class="cap">{covered(r) ? "filmed elsewhere" : "filmed by nobody"}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>

  <div class="one" style="margin-top:44px">
    <div class="lab">The draft, in Croatian</div>
    <div class="prose" style="margin-top:8px" set:html={mdp(
`*Poštovani, u Vašem popisu matičnih knjiga navedeno je da sljedeće knjige nisu digitalizirane: ____. Molim Vas obavijest o mogućnosti uvida ili naručivanja preslika upisa za prezime **De Franceschi / Defranceschi**, uz signaturu knjige. Unaprijed zahvaljujem.*

**Fill the blank from the tables above** — the DAPA number and the years are what the office works from. The archive's [errands page](/errands/) carries the ones already sent and what came back; DAPA has answered before and asks for a completed request form, which needs personal data this archive does not hold.`)}></div>
  </div>

  <p class="cap" style="margin-top:36px">
    Source: Državni arhiv u Pazinu's own register list, held at <code>site/src/data/registers.json</code> — {registers.length} entries, of which {rows.length} are marked not digitised.
    <a href={u("/map/dapa/")}>Pazin on the research map →</a> ·
    <a href={u("/parish-books/")}>The parish books →</a>
  </p>
</Base>
